WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
I built this system to turn public evidence into reviewable decisions.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.100
This run asks what a customer-side Drata Administrator does.

3
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.840
It starts with a precise role brief and current official documentation.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:15.080
The live pipeline completed eleven stages in just over twenty-eight minutes.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.460
It normalized role, population, scope, and evidence rules into structured input.

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.980
No automated stage grants approval. Human approvals in this run are zero.

7
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.200
Research targeted vendor documentation that could support specific administrator tasks.

8
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.740
Twelve official pages were fetched live, with excerpts checked against their exact pages.

9
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:38.340
Ten source-bound evidence items were accepted. Two failed exact-source checks and were quarantined.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.420
Eight retained synthesis sources shaped the draft. Retained does not mean independently validated.

11
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:49.340
Exact quote matching protects provenance, but cannot prove every generated claim is semantically supported.

12
00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.260
From that evidence, the Pre-JTA proposed twenty-two tasks across five domains.

13
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.880
Three simulated reviewers challenged it: devil's advocate, fictional SME panel, and bias-and-fairness review.

14
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:06.600
They disagreed on priorities, frequency, company size, enterprise controls, and international coverage.

15
00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.840
The system preserved disagreement and documented every reconciliation decision.

16
00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.640
The result was twenty draft tasks across five domains, with fourteen documented changes.

17
00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:22.480
It reduced the weakest domain's provisional weight, consolidated thin tasks, simplified language, and flagged shared-role work.

18
00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:29.900
The domains cover access, governance, connections, controls and evidence, and access-review personnel data.

19
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.840
The capability layer then produced fourteen subdomains and sixty KSAs.

20
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.280
That is twenty-five knowledge statements, twenty-one skills, and fourteen abilities.

21
00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.580
Every KSA stays in a known domain, and every task reference resolves.

22
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:47.480
Each accepted item keeps its URL, excerpt, receipt file, and receipt hash.

23
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.780
A separate pass ran three hundred ninety-seven structural and source checks. All passed.

24
00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.400
They covered allowlists, quote spans, stable IDs, domain membership, and task-to-KSA links.

25
00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:02.000
Those checks prove consistency and traceability. They do not equal human validation.

26
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.300
Every weight, frequency, criticality rating, confidence value, and reviewer judgment remains provisional.

27
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:14.060
No practitioner interviews, job-posting corroboration, observed frequencies, signed-in lesson evidence, or pilots were included.

28
00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:18.480
This is an unapproved draft, not an exam, credential, or compliance assurance.

29
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.400
It is independent work, not affiliated with, endorsed by, or reviewed by Drata.

30
00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:29.720
Example tasks cover Admin roles, least-privilege connections, control evidence, and access-review personnel data.

31
00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:34.000
KSAs cover permissions, service accounts, and choosing evidence types for controls.

32
00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.120
The public report shows accepted source links and exact excerpts for inspection.

33
00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:43.540
Next, real administrators must validate tasks, identify gaps, and challenge every provisional rating.

34
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:49.100
Human semantic evidence review, accessibility review, and publication approval must happen before assessment design.
